<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan auctions bonds worth 1.3 bln rupees.</title>
<headline>Pakistan auctions bonds worth 1.3 bln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The State (central) Bank of Pakistan said it had auctioned six-month maturity short-term federal bonds worth more than 1.3 billion rupees on Monday at a weighted average yield of 17.0676 percent per annum.</p>
<p>The bank received bids worth a total of 2,959.01 million rupees, of which bids for 1,339.01 million rupees were accepted.</p>
<p>In the previous auction held on March 27, bids worth 162.25 million rupees were accepted at a weighted average yield of 16.9401 percent per annum.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
